directory commands
whoami : it itewlls which user you are using right now

echo: output some specific text that provider => echo "hello world!"

cat : show the content of a file => cat notepad.txt

cd : change directory => cd ./my-directory

ls: show list of files => ls , ls -a : it show also hidden files

pwd: it prints all way to current directory

find : search for file by their name => find -name pasword.txt

grep : search inside for text for example => grep "pasword123" pasword.txt

touch : create file => touch note.txt

cp: copy file => cp note.txt | cp note.txt ./newfolder

mv: move or rename file and directory => mv note.txt ../ |  mv note.text rename.txt

rm : remove file or directory